WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.531
If your account receives a performance notification, it means Amazon has detected violations of

00:00:07.531 --> 00:00:15.600
one or more of Amazon's selling policies, applicable law, or the seller code of conduct.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:23.040
Depending on the severity of the violation, Amazon may remove your listings or deactivate your account.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:30.040
It's important to address any violations immediately to maintain your selling privileges in the

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:31.040
Amazon store.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:37.340
Additionally, ensure that your business partners, employees, and any third-party partners you work

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:40.040
with understand and follow these policies.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:47.540
To review all your performance notifications by date, open the main menu in Seller Central.

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:51.040
Hover over Performance and select Performance Notifications.

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:57.356
Each notification includes the action taken on your account and the information needed to appeal

00:00:57.356 --> 00:00:59.040
or dispute that action.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:06.619
To address a policy violation, open the main menu in Seller Central, hover over Performance and

00:01:06.619 --> 00:01:08.040
select Account Health.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:13.707
From the Account Health dashboard, select the name of the policy issue that has been violated from

00:01:13.707 --> 00:01:15.040
the Policy Compliance section.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:23.040
You'll see a list of each violation, the date, affected ASINs, Amazon's actions, and next steps.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:28.040
To review the violated policy, select the link under the Reason column.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:34.040
To take action on a violation, click the Submit Appeal button under the Next Steps column.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:38.040
If you understand the violation, take the necessary steps to correct the issue.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:44.707
For example, if your product detail page doesn't comply with Amazon's policies, update the listing

00:01:44.707 --> 00:01:46.040
to meet requirements.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:51.665
Select "I understand the policy" and acknowledge the violation and input the primary reasons for

00:01:51.665 --> 00:01:58.040
the root cause or the violation as well as all actions you've taken to correct the issue.

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:05.973
If you believe the notification was sent in error, select "I understand the policy" and have evidence

00:02:05.973 --> 00:02:12.040
or documentation to submit for review to confirm my compliance with the policy.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:19.071
Select the appropriate fields that accurately describe the error and upload any evidence or documentation

00:02:19.071 --> 00:02:25.165
that demonstrates that your account complies with Amazon's customer product reviews policies and

00:02:25.165 --> 00:02:27.040
seller code of conduct.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:32.040
If your appeal is successful, your listing will be reactivated.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:38.040
We'll contact you via email with our decision and let you know if we require more information.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:44.040
This might be a letter of authorization, invoices, or additional compliance documents.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:50.897
Return to the Performance Notifications page at any time to reference your appeal status and any

00:02:50.897 --> 00:02:53.040
correspondence between you and Amazon.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:59.997
If the violation led to deactivation of your account, select "Reactivate Your Account" on the Account

00:02:59.997 --> 00:03:03.040
Health page and follow the provided instructions.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:07.040
Note that this information does not constitute legal advice.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:13.882
For additional information about customer product reviews policies, visit the Customer Product Reviews

00:03:13.882 --> 00:03:17.040
Policies Help page in Seller Central.
